    {
      "name": "gitea",
      "language": "Go",
      "notes": "go-sdk's TestPull panics against its own release, Gitea 1.24.2, in CI (pull_test.go:105 dereferences a pull request the mergeability check did not return), and a panic ends the test binary, so every test after it went unrun in arm a. It is skipped by name; it would fail arm a and be left out anyway. 1.23.7 -> 1.24.2, with go-sdk 0.22.0, the release that tested 1.23.7, was run (Actions run 35917620682) and broke nothing the suite exercises, so it is not kept.",
      "repo": "go-gitea/gitea",
      "image": "gitea/gitea",
      "server": {
        "port": 3000,
        "ready": "/api/v1/version",
        "readySeconds": 300,
        "env": {
          "GITEA__security__INSTALL_LOCK": "true",
          "GITEA__security__PASSWORD_COMPLEXITY": "off",
          "GITEA__security__MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH": "6",
          "GITEA__database__DB_TYPE": "sqlite3",
          "GITEA__server__ROOT_URL": "http://gitea:3000/",
          "GITEA__service__DISABLE_REGISTRATION": "false"
        },
        "setup": [
          {
            "run": [
              "docker",
              "exec",
              "-u",
              "git",
              "{container}",
              "gitea",
              "admin",
              "user",
              "create",
              "--username=test01",
              "--password={GITEA_PASSWORD}",
              "--email=test01@gitea.io",
              "--admin=true",
              "--must-change-password=false",
              "--access-token"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secrets": {
          "GITEA_PASSWORD": {
            "random": 16
          }
        }
      },
      "spec": {
        "served": "/swagger.v1.json"
      },
      "suite": {
        "repo": "https://gitea.com/gitea/go-sdk.git",
        "sparse": [],
        "dir": "gitea",
        "install": [["go", "mod", "download"]],
        "run": [
          "go",
          "run",
          "gotest.tools/gotestsum@v1.13.0",
          "--junitfile",
          "{report}",
          "--",
          "-skip",
          "^TestPull$",
          "-count=1",
          "."
        ],
        "select": ["-run", "{select}"],
        "env": {
          "GITEA_SDK_TEST_URL": "{url}",
          "GITEA_SDK_TEST_USERNAME": "test01",
          "GITEA_SDK_TEST_PASSWORD": "{GITEA_PASSWORD}"
        }
      },
      "releases": {
        "v1.24.2": {
          "commit": "acd4e10990e63f0f81ecb0252b8f5c044cb6df0e",
          "digest": "sha256:8e2e3f40c5ff3fee920c6d0faac0db9cca2183d80ff23965d1022434d37e7910",
          "suite": "060554f46291abccac23a24f5e9bb264f962e21d",
          "suiteRef": "refs/tags/gitea/v0.22.1"
        },
        "v1.25.4": {
          "commit": "369830bada2fd8826a5135cb2fc66660a9bef708",
          "digest": "sha256:17d18218be2dad1f8ed402a4f906989505c90ab8b66ee9befcecfb5d470133e7"
        }
      },
      "pairs": [["v1.24.2", "v1.25.4"]]
    },
    {
      "name": "immich",
      "language": "TypeScript",
      "notes": "The suite is Immich's own end-to-end API specs (e2e/src/api), which call 127.0.0.1:2285 and reach the database on 127.0.0.1:5435 themselves, so the server answers on the port the suite names and the proxy takes it in arm c. The CLI and immich-admin specs are left out: they run the release's command-line tools rather than calling the API.",
      "repo": "immich-app/immich",
      "image": "ghcr.io/immich-app/immich-server",
      "server": {
        "port": 2285,
        "suitePort": 2285,
        "ready": "/api/server/ping",
        "readySeconds": 300,
        "compose": "compose/immich.yaml",
        "secrets": {
          "IMMICH_DB_PASSWORD": {
            "suite": "src/utils.ts",
            "pattern": "postgres://postgres:([^@]+)@127\\.0\\.0\\.1:5435/immich"
          }
        }
      },
      "spec": {
        "path": "open-api/immich-openapi-specs.json"
      },
      "suite": {
        "sparse": [
          "e2e",
          "open-api/typescript-sdk",
          "cli",
          "open-api/immich-openapi-specs.json",
          ".gitmodules"
        ],
        "submodules": ["e2e/test-assets"],
        "dir": "e2e",
        "install": [
          [
            "npm",
            "ci",
            "--prefix",
            "../open-api/typescript-sdk",
            "--no-audit",
            "--no-fund"
          ],
          ["npm", "run", "build", "--prefix", "../open-api/typescript-sdk"],
          ["npm", "ci", "--no-audit", "--no-fund"]
        ],
        "run": [
          "npx",
          "vitest",
          "run",
          "src/api",
          "--reporter=default",
          "--reporter=junit",
          "--outputFile.junit={report}"
        ],
        "select": ["-t", "{select}"],
        "env": {}
      },
      "releases": {
        "v1.137.3": {
          "commit": "007ba1d9efdc571c87ca1553dd28dbbfe7eeee2f",
          "digest": "sha256:e517f806457057d44695152a0af2dfa094225a7d85eb37f518925e68864c658d"
        },
        "v1.138.0": {
          "commit": "bede19a3ca48c2c0465c7fb80fdc8d36ec428aa0",
          "digest": "sha256:12cee930e2cc211a95acae12ad780c0b2eecaea0479a06e255c73a4deb0b3efb"
        }
      },
      "pairs": [["v1.137.3", "v1.138.0"]]
    }
  ],
  "skipped": [
    {
      "name": "jellyfin",
      "language": "C#",
      "reason": "Specifications are published for every release and 10.11 -> 12.0 really breaks (routes removed, SessionInfo.NowPlayingQueueFullItems gone), but no suite of a 10.11 release exercises it: jellyfin-sdk-typescript v0.13.0's five live tests touch no changed operation, the Kotlin, C# and Python SDKs have only mocked tests, and the server's own integration tests run in-process against test-only controllers."
    },
    {
      "name": "keycloak",
      "language": "Java",
      "reason": "Every ERR-level delta between consecutive published admin API specifications (24.0.5 to 26.7.4) is a documentation fix (a status the server already returned, a renamed path parameter, a schema renamed to its existing wire name); the real breaks (identity providers leaving the realm representation, locked-out users reporting enabled, brief organization members) are behavioral and absent from the specification."
    },
    {
      "name": "directus",
      "language": "TypeScript",
      "reason": "No release pair has a structural REST break that its own suite both exercises and passes on the old release: the 11.0 policies change is behavioral and crashes the blackbox seeds before any REST call, 11.0 to 11.4 fail arm a (upstream patched the suite in 11.4.1), and the later breaks (/webhooks, /utils/hash removed, /server/health auth, inactive collections) are unexercised or behavioral."
    },
    {
      "name": "forgejo",
      "language": "Go",
      "reason": "No live-instance suite fails because of an ERR-level delta: the Forgejo specification barely changes on the wire from 7 to 16. The one exercised break found (9.0 refusing a token with no scopes, which fails forgejo-sdk v1.2.0's TestUserApp) is absent from the specification, whose CreateAccessTokenOption is identical in 8.0.3 and 9.0.3."
    },
    {
      "name": "appwrite",
      "language": "PHP",
      "reason": "1.9.0 -> 1.9.5 renames webhook fields and moves a route, which the ops serve, but two of the tests it breaks are behavioral (the signature key is no longer returned on GET, and a filter names the old field inside a query string), so the pair cannot be served in full. Its suite also runs only from a development image built from source, against the fixed host http://appwrite/v1. Not wired yet."
    },
    {
      "name": "openmetadata",
      "language": "Java",
      "reason": "1.4.8 -> 1.5.0 renames owner to owners and makes it a list, which move and wrapArray serve, but the Python SDK that is the suite refuses on connect any server whose minor version differs from its own, so arm c cannot run without falsifying the version the server reports."
    }
  ]
}
